  <prompt>Close the unified-access-control-r2 project: run the mandatory /test-diet gate, close out design-register hygiene items H-8a and H-8b, disposition every defer/issue register entry under the owner's 2026-09-15 rule, write lessons-learned, flip the README to Complete, and reconcile TASK-INDEX/current-task. Follow root CLAUDE.md §7's project-close protocol exactly.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Project closure procedures. Follow root CLAUDE.md §7 strictly.</role>
  <goal>test-diet report generated and cited; H-8a/H-8b closed (or explicitly re-dispositioned with rationale); every notes/defer-issues.md entry closed or handed off under the 2026-09-15 rule, in sync with its GitHub issue; notes/lessons-learned.md written; README status Complete with summary; TASK-INDEX all-green; current-task.md reset to "none"; wrap-up PR cites the test-diet report and the register disposition table.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Root CLAUDE.md §7 project-close test diet gate (BINDING): task-execute Step 11 invokes /test-diet BEFORE marking the project complete; skipping is a HARD WARNING and the wrap-up PR MUST cite the report or document the skip rationale. Register items: H-8a = stale comments naming the deleted ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter/ExternalCallerContext (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:13,24,339 — plus the further grep hits: ExternalDataService.cs:16, ExternalCallerContext.cs:7, ExternalUserContextEndpoint.cs:14,18, ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:52); H-8b = RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:182 returns vestigial WebRoleRemoved: false (Power Pages relic, Dtos/RevokeAccessResponse.cs) and retains a best-effort SPE-permission-removal path — H-8b was flagged "related to A-13 (FR-16), fix together", so FIRST verify what the Phase 0 FR-16 task already did and close only the remainder. Defer/issue register: notes/defer-issues.md carries a Disposition table (added 2026-09-15); the project label `unified-access-control-r2` is the GitHub rollup (`gh issue list --state all --label unified-access-control-r2`).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs (H-8a comments)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs + ExternalCallerContext.cs (H-8a comments)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalUserContextEndpoint.cs (H-8a comments)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs + Dtos/RevokeAccessResponse.cs (H-8b)</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/defer-issues.md (disposition gate)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/lessons-learned.md</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/unified-access-control-r2/README.md</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md + current-task.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="083" status="pending">Last phase task; all phases complete before closure.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§7">/test-diet runs BEFORE completion; it is read-only (emits git rm/git mv for the reviewer — do NOT auto-execute deletions); the wrap-up PR cites projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/test-diet-report.md. Scope: closure sequence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-15">Scope: every defer/issue register entry. An entry leaves this project ONLY if (a) it is not material to the project, with the evidence recorded, or (b) another project's ownership of its subject matter is confirmed (named project + evidence). Otherwise it is fixed in this project before closure. When materiality is unclear, it stays. "Handed off" is recorded in the register AND as a comment on the GitHub issue; an entry handed off with no confirmed owner is named as such in the wrap-up PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">H-8a is comment-only: no behavioural edits ride along under the cleanup banner. Scope: every H-8a file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">H-8b: removing WebRoleRemoved from RevokeAccessResponse is an API-contract change — grep ALL clients (AccessGrantModal, SPA, Teams) for consumers of the field first; if any consumer reads it, coordinate the removal or keep the field with a deprecation comment and record the decision. Scope: the DTO edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">The H-8x edits touch BFF files: verify build + report publish size in the PR even for cleanup. Scope: PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§7">Completion order: task poml statuses -> TASK-INDEX -> current-task reset -> README -> report. Scope: closure sequence.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>project closure</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/design-register.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/defer-issues.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/project-defer-issue-tracking/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="repo-cleanup" location=".claude/skills/repo-cleanup/SKILL.md">Ephemeral-file hygiene at close.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration. Verify every task in TASK-INDEX is ✅ (or explicitly deferred with a note) — if not, STOP: this task's gate is unmet.</step>
    <step order="1">Defer/issue disposition gate: reconcile notes/defer-issues.md with `gh issue list --state all --label unified-access-control-r2` (every register entry has an issue; every labelled issue has an entry). For each entry not Done: it is either fixed here (STOP — the gate is unmet) or handed off under the 2026-09-15 rule with its evidence recorded and a comment on the issue. Status and issue state agree.</step>
    <step order="2">Invoke /test-diet; review the classification; save the report; do NOT execute deletions — hand the emitted commands to the reviewer via the PR.</step>
    <step order="3">H-8a: remove/replace the stale ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter/ExternalCallerContext comment references (grep-verified complete list); comment-only diff.</step>
    <step order="4">H-8b: check FR-16's (A-13) merged fix; then remove the vestigial WebRoleRemoved field + dead SPE-removal remainder per the consumer-grep constraint; document the disposition.</step>
    <step order="5">Write notes/lessons-learned.md: what the investigation-first approach caught (F1 refutation shaping FR-26), the reclassification of the BU restructure to UAT, the POA consolidation reuse story, evaluator-versioning decisions, and process lessons for the next access project.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify success criteria 1-9 in spec.md each have their verification pointer (test name / UAT item); record the mapping in the README status section.</step>
    <step order="7">Update README to Complete; reconcile TASK-INDEX; reset current-task.md to "none"; build green; publish size reported.</step>
    <step order="8">Wrap-up PR citing the test-diet report, the register closeouts and the defer/issue disposition table (naming any hand-off that has no confirmed owner).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If H-8b's WebRoleRemoved field is read by ANY client, or the SPE-removal path turns out to be live behaviour post-FR-16, STOP the removal and record a path-A disposition (kept + deprecated, reason documented) instead — a wrap-up task must not ship a breaking contract change.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any defer/issue entry is material to this project and not Done, STOP — the project does not close with it open. Escalate to the owner only to confirm a hand-off, never to skip the entry.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/lessons-learned.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/test-diet-report.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/defer-issues.md (every entry Done or handed off)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/README.md (status Complete)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ (H-8a/H-8b cleanups)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every notes/defer-issues.md entry is Done, Won't Fix (with a decision record) or handed off under the 2026-09-15 rule with its evidence; no entry material to this project is open; every entry's GitHub issue is labelled `unified-access-control-r2` and its state matches the register.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/test-diet-report.md exists and is cited in the wrap-up PR description; no test deletion was auto-executed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep for ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter across src/ returns zero comment references (H-8a closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H-8b dispositioned: either WebRoleRemoved removed with consumer-grep evidence, or kept-deprecated with the documented reason; the design register updated either way.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/lessons-learned.md exists with the five content areas from step 5.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">README status Complete incl. success-criteria mapping; TASK-INDEX fully reconciled; current-task.md reads "none".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: build green after the H-8x edits; no behavioural test changes required by them (proving cleanup-only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Root CLAUDE.md §7 (test-diet gate is BINDING). UAT items (BU restructure, live-dev secure verification) remain open in notes/phase4-uat-acceptance.md — the README must link them as post-project environment work, not silently absorb them.

AMENDED 2026-09-15 — owner rule for the register: "issues should only go past the project if they are not material to the project or they are confirmed/validated as another project's subject matter." Added the disposition gate (step 1, constraint, criterion, second escalation trigger) and deps 099, 101, 104–107.</notes>

